   "plaque": "arts_angelas_ashes",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "Angela's Ashes",
   "text": "Frank McCourt was born in Brooklyn in 1930 and brought back to Limerick as a small boy, to the lanes, the damp and the hunger of the 1930s. He taught in New York schools for thirty years and then, at 66, published Angela's Ashes, which won the Pulitzer Prize in 1997 and sold in its millions. Limerick was not sure about it at first. He died in 2009, and the city that gave him the childhood now gives him a museum, which is the kind of ending he would have found funny."
